  "body": "Privately positioned up a sweeping driveway and occupying an expansive 1,945sqm (approx.) site, this substantial Adrian Robinson-designed residence is a home of enduring quality, exceptional scale, and remarkable versatility. Spanning approximately 569sqm across two generous levels, the home has been thoughtfully designed to accommodate the evolving needs of family life, offering an outstanding balance of togetherness, privacy, and flexibility.\r\n\r\nA sense of scale is immediate upon arrival. The grand entrance hall and impressive staircase introduce a series of beautifully proportioned living spaces, where formal and informal lounges and dining areas flow seamlessly together. French doors open to sun-soaked terraces and private outdoor entertaining areas, creating effortless connections between indoors and out. Whether hosting on a grand scale or enjoying everyday family life, the layout has been carefully considered to provide spaces to gather, entertain, work, and retreat.\r\n\r\nAccommodation is exceptionally generous, with six bedrooms offering remarkable flexibility for families of all stages. The upper level is dedicated primarily to family living, featuring four spacious bedrooms, including a luxurious primary suite complete with an expansive ensuite and walk-in wardrobe. The master suite enjoys access to a sunny terrace, also shared with an adjacent bedroom, creating a peaceful retreat overlooking the grounds. On the lower level, two further bedrooms provide excellent separation, one with its own ensuite - ideal for guests, extended family, or multigenerational living.\r\n\r\nBuilt of concrete block with a solid stucco exterior, the home is a residence of genuine substance, complemented by three bathrooms, two guest powder rooms on the main living level, a dedicated study or office, sauna, full laundry, and secure three-car garaging.\r\n\r\nThe expansive grounds enhance the sense of privacy and tranquillity, offering ample space for children to play, future landscaping aspirations, or simply enjoying the peace and seclusion of this remarkable setting.\r\n\r\nA home of genuine presence and distinction, 30 Dingle Road offers a rare combination of size, privacy, enduring quality, and position. Moments from the waterfront and within sought-after school zones including St Heliers School, St Ignatius Catholic School, Glendowie College, and Baradene College, this is an exceptional opportunity to secure one of the Bays' most significant family homes.\r\n\r\n- \r\n\r\nRichard Thode has established himself as one of the outstanding performers within Ray White, both in New Zealand and internationally. Carey Smith, Joint Chairman of the Ray White Group, says \"His results are exceptional, but what has impressed me most is the consistency, drive and professionalism behind those results. Richard combines strong commercial instincts and outstanding negotiation skills with a genuine commitment to his clients. As Ray White's number one salesperson in New Zealand and one of our leading performers internationally, Richard has demonstrated an ability to perform at the very highest level year after year. I have no hesitation in recommending Richard to clients considering selling their property.\"",
